{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLValidator\/Issue"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Issue"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"mentions":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/UsingIvorMXL"],"kind":"mentions"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An issue describes conformance the schema cannot express and the parser"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"does not enforce. The catalogue is deliberately confined to checks that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"sound on conforming input"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" — a well-formed score never trips one —"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so that a reported issue is always a genuine defect and never a false"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"alarm. Every check runs against the normalized part-wise score, so "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"part"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"measure"},{"type":"text","text":" labels are the part "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"id"},{"type":"text","text":" and measure "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"number"},{"type":"text","text":" from that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"score."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An opus is not checked at all: its schema is four elements and the parser"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"already enforces nearly everything they constrain, so it passes straight"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"through the validator."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Two checks the schema-diff proposal listed as candidates are deliberately"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"absent, because they cannot be decided soundly from the AST alone:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Measure duration versus the prevailing "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<time>"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"text","text":" MusicXML permits"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"partial measures that are not flagged "},{"code":"implicit","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (pickups, measures split"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"across a repeat or a mid-measure meter change), so a short measure is not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"evidence of a defect."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Number-keyed spanner pairing ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<slur>"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<tuplet>"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<wedge>"},{"type":"text","text":", and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"like)."}]},{"type":"text","text":" The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"number"},{"type":"text","text":" level is reused across simultaneous voices, and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"spec expressly allows a spanner’s start and stop to appear in arbitrary"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"document order, so pairing them requires the per-voice onset timeline the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"resolver builds — not something the validator can settle. Unclosed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"spanners are also a common, non-fatal real-world imperfection."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]}]}],"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/